{"title":"Career Roadmap: Music Composer","role":"Music Composer","summary":"The composer converts an idea, emotion, story or creative brief into a musical work.","facts":{"Current degree":"BA (Bachelor of Arts - General / Honours)","Course":"Music (Vocal / Instrumental)"},"about":[{"label":"Primary Goal","text":"Develop strong musical foundations, composition, arranging, orchestration, music technology, recording and professional portfolio skills"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Roadmap Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Music Composer creates original music for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Films"},{"text":"Web series"},{"text":"Television"},{"text":"Games"},{"text":"Advertisements"},{"text":"Albums"},{"text":"Independent artists"},{"text":"Theatre"},{"text":"Documentaries"},{"text":"Podcasts"},{"text":"Digital content"},{"text":"Live performances"},{"text":"Background scores"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The composer converts an idea, emotion, story or creative brief into a musical work."},{"type":"p","text":"A typical workflow is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Brief/Concept","Musical Idea","Melody","Harmony/Rhythm","Arrangement","Instrumentation","Production","Recording","Mixing","Mastering","Delivery"]},{"type":"p","text":"A BA in Music provides the musical foundation, but professional employability increasingly requires a combination of:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Music Theory","Composition","Arrangement","Instrumental/Vocal Skills","DAW Production","Portfolio","Collaboration"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"What to Build During UG","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Build This","Learn From","Proof of Skill","Gap to Avoid"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Music fundamentals"},{"text":"Theory, ear training, instrument/voice"},{"text":"Short compositions"},{"text":"Only performing without composing"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Composition & arrangement"},{"text":"Harmony, rhythm, orchestration"},{"text":"Original music portfolio"},{"text":"Limited musical vocabulary"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Music production"},{"text":"DAWs, recording, mixing"},{"text":"Produced tracks"},{"text":"No technology skills"}],[{"text":"Year 4*"},{"text":"Professional composition"},{"text":"Film/game/ad scoring, collaboration"},{"text":"Demo reel + internship"},{"text":"No finished commercial-style work"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"*For a 4-year honours structure. In a 3-year BA, incorporate the advanced production objectives into the final year."}]},{"heading":"Semester-by-Semester Roadmap","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Semester 1 — Musical Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Music notation"},{"text":"Rhythm"},{"text":"Melody"},{"text":"Scales"},{"text":"Modes"},{"text":"Intervals"},{"text":"Chords"},{"text":"Tempo"},{"text":"Dynamics"},{"text":"Musical form"},{"text":"Ear training"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Develop proficiency in at least one primary:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Vocal music"},{"text":"Piano/keyboard"},{"text":"Guitar"},{"text":"Violin"},{"text":"Indian classical instrument"},{"text":"Western classical instrument"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The primary instrument becomes an important composition and arrangement tool."},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 2 — Harmony & Musical Language"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"h","text":"Harmony"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Triads"},{"text":"Seventh chords"},{"text":"Chord progressions"},{"text":"Cadences"},{"text":"Voice leading"},{"text":"Modulation"},{"text":"Tonality"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Melody"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Motifs"},{"text":"Phrases"},{"text":"Repetition"},{"text":"Variation"},{"text":"Countermelody"},{"text":"Call and response"},{"text":"Melodic development"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Rhythm"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Meter"},{"text":"Syncopation"},{"text":"Polyrhythm"},{"text":"Groove"},{"text":"Tempo changes"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Practice writing short pieces every week."},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 3 — Composition"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn different forms:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Binary"},{"text":"Ternary"},{"text":"Rondo"},{"text":"Theme and variations"},{"text":"Verse-chorus"},{"text":"AABA"},{"text":"Through-composed"},{"text":"Suite"},{"text":"Song forms"},{"text":"Film-score structures"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Practice composing for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Solo instrument"},{"text":"Voice"},{"text":"Small ensemble"},{"text":"Piano"},{"text":"Electronic instruments"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Build a library of musical motifs and themes."}]},{"heading":"Indian & Western Music","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A strong composer can benefit from understanding multiple musical systems."},{"type":"h","text":"Indian Music"},{"type":"p","text":"Depending on specialization:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Raga"},{"text":"Tala"},{"text":"Shruti"},{"text":"Improvisation"},{"text":"Gamaka"},{"text":"Hindustani traditions"},{"text":"Carnatic traditions"},{"text":"Folk traditions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Western Music"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Major/minor systems"},{"text":"Harmony"},{"text":"Counterpoint"},{"text":"Chord progressions"},{"text":"Orchestration"},{"text":"Classical forms"},{"text":"Contemporary composition"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The goal is not to superficially learn everything, but to develop a deep primary musical identity with broader musical vocabulary."}]},{"heading":"Semester 4 — Arrangement & Orchestration","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn how to turn a musical idea into a complete arrangement."},{"type":"h","text":"Arrangement"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Instrument selection"},{"text":"Register"},{"text":"Voicing"},{"text":"Layering"},{"text":"Dynamics"},{"text":"Texture"},{"text":"Groove"},{"text":"Transitions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Orchestration"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn the characteristics of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Strings"},{"text":"Woodwinds"},{"text":"Brass"},{"text":"Percussion"},{"text":"Piano"},{"text":"Guitar"},{"text":"Bass"},{"text":"Synthesizers"},{"text":"Indian instruments"},{"text":"Choir"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the range and expressive characteristics of each instrument."}]},{"heading":"Music for Different Media","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A composer should learn how music changes according to the medium."},{"type":"h","text":"Film/TV"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Background score"},{"text":"Themes"},{"text":"Character motifs"},{"text":"Emotional scoring"},{"text":"Scene transitions"},{"text":"Action sequences"},{"text":"Dramatic tension"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Games"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Interactive music"},{"text":"Loops"},{"text":"Adaptive scoring"},{"text":"Game-state transitions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Advertising"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Short musical ideas"},{"text":"Brand themes"},{"text":"Sonic logos"},{"text":"Jingles"},{"text":"Emotional hooks"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Podcasts"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Intro music"},{"text":"Outro"},{"text":"Background beds"},{"text":"Transitions"},{"text":"Sonic branding"}]}]},{"heading":"Film Scoring","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn the relationship between:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Story","Scene","Emotion","Musical Theme","Arrangement","Synchronization"]},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Spotting"},{"text":"Cue sheets"},{"text":"Scene timing"},{"text":"Character themes"},{"text":"Leitmotifs"},{"text":"Tension"},{"text":"Release"},{"text":"Transitions"},{"text":"Underscore"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Practice scoring short scenes from copyright-cleared or self-created footage."}]},{"heading":"Music Production","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Modern composers should understand digital production."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"DAWs"},{"text":"MIDI"},{"text":"Virtual instruments"},{"text":"Sampling"},{"text":"Synthesizers"},{"text":"Audio recording"},{"text":"Editing"},{"text":"Arrangement"},{"text":"Automation"},{"text":"Effects"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Popular DAWs include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Logic Pro"},{"text":"Ableton Live"},{"text":"FL Studio"},{"text":"Cubase"},{"text":"Pro Tools"},{"text":"Studio One"},{"text":"Reaper"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A student does not need every DAW. Master one primary DAW."}]},{"heading":"Sound Design","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Synthesis"},{"text":"Sampling"},{"text":"Foley awareness"},{"text":"Ambience"},{"text":"Textures"},{"text":"Risers"},{"text":"Impacts"},{"text":"Drones"},{"text":"Electronic sound design"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Oscillators"},{"text":"Filters"},{"text":"Envelopes"},{"text":"LFOs"},{"text":"ADSR"},{"text":"Subtractive synthesis"},{"text":"Sampling"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Sound design is especially useful for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Films"},{"text":"Games"},{"text":"Advertisements"},{"text":"Digital media"}]}]},{"heading":"Recording","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn basic recording techniques."},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Microphone types"},{"text":"Microphone placement"},{"text":"Gain staging"},{"text":"Recording levels"},{"text":"Room acoustics"},{"text":"Noise"},{"text":"Monitoring"},{"text":"Audio interfaces"},{"text":"Headphones"},{"text":"Studio monitors"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For vocal/instrumental recording, practice:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Record","Edit","Clean","Arrange","Mix"]}]},{"heading":"Mixing","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop basic competence in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"EQ"},{"text":"Compression"},{"text":"Reverb"},{"text":"Delay"},{"text":"Panning"},{"text":"Automation"},{"text":"Stereo imaging"},{"text":"Gain staging"},{"text":"Bus processing"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Frequency balance"},{"text":"Dynamic range"},{"text":"Headroom"},{"text":"Clipping"},{"text":"Loudness"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The composer does not necessarily need to become a specialist mix engineer, but should be able to deliver professional demos and communicate effectively with engineers."}]},{"heading":"Mastering Awareness","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Loudness"},{"text":"Peak levels"},{"text":"Dynamic range"},{"text":"Stereo"},{"text":"File formats"},{"text":"Sample rate"},{"text":"Bit depth"},{"text":"Delivery specifications"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand common delivery formats such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"WAV"},{"text":"MP3"},{"text":"AIFF"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For professional work, final delivery requirements should always follow the client/platform specification."}]},{"heading":"Digital Audio Fundamentals","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sample rate"},{"text":"Bit depth"},{"text":"MIDI"},{"text":"Audio vs MIDI"},{"text":"Mono vs stereo"},{"text":"Lossy vs lossless formats"},{"text":"Latency"},{"text":"Digital clipping"},{"text":"Signal flow"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the difference between:"},{"type":"h","text":"MIDI note data ≠ recorded audio"},{"type":"p","text":"This distinction is fundamental to digital composition."}]},{"heading":"AI & Music Technology","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A modern composer should understand AI-assisted music workflows."},{"type":"p","text":"Explore:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI-assisted ideation"},{"text":"MIDI generation"},{"text":"Arrangement assistance"},{"text":"Stem separation"},{"text":"Audio restoration"},{"text":"Transcription"},{"text":"Sound-design assistance"},{"text":"Voice/audio processing"},{"text":"Music analysis"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Important issues:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Copyright"},{"text":"Training-data concerns"},{"text":"Ownership"},{"text":"Licensing"},{"text":"Consent"},{"text":"Artist rights"},{"text":"Dataset provenance"}]},{"type":"p","text":"AI-generated material should not be assumed to be commercially safe simply because a tool produced it. Always verify the applicable platform licence and rights before commercial use."}]},{"heading":"Music Business","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A professional composer needs business knowledge."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Music publishing"},{"text":"Copyright"},{"text":"Performance rights"},{"text":"Mechanical rights"},{"text":"Synchronization rights"},{"text":"Master rights"},{"text":"Composition rights"},{"text":"Licensing"},{"text":"Royalties"},{"text":"Contracts"},{"text":"Work-for-hire concepts"},{"text":"Credits"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the difference between:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Composition","Recording/Master","Performance","Synchronization"]},{"type":"p","text":"These rights can involve different stakeholders."},{"type":"p","text":"For actual contracts or rights disputes, professional legal advice is appropriate."}]},{"heading":"Professional Collaboration","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Composers regularly collaborate with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Directors"},{"text":"Producers"},{"text":"Lyricists"},{"text":"Singers"},{"text":"Musicians"},{"text":"Arrangers"},{"text":"Sound designers"},{"text":"Mix engineers"},{"text":"Mastering engineers"},{"text":"Game developers"},{"text":"Advertisers"},{"text":"Content creators"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Develop:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Brief interpretation"},{"text":"Feedback handling"},{"text":"Version management"},{"text":"Deadline management"},{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"File organization"}]}]},{"heading":"Music Portfolio Strategy","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A composer should not rely on a single genre."},{"type":"p","text":"Build a varied demo reel containing:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Film score"},{"text":"Emotional piano/orchestral piece"},{"text":"Commercial/jingle"},{"text":"Contemporary song"},{"text":"Electronic composition"},{"text":"Game-style track"},{"text":"Regional/Indian-inspired composition"},{"text":"Vocal arrangement"},{"text":"Instrumental composition"},{"text":"Experimental piece"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The exact portfolio should be adapted to the target career specialization."}]},{"heading":"Projects to Build","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — Original Music EP"},{"type":"p","text":"Create:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"4–6 original compositions"},{"text":"Different moods/styles"},{"text":"Professional arrangements"},{"text":"Basic mixing"},{"text":"Cover artwork"},{"text":"Metadata"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Document:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Concept"},{"text":"Composition process"},{"text":"Instrumentation"},{"text":"Production approach"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — Short Film Scoring"},{"type":"p","text":"Take a short copyright-cleared or self-created film."},{"type":"p","text":"Create:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Spotting notes"},{"text":"Musical themes"},{"text":"Multiple cues"},{"text":"Scene transitions"},{"text":"Final synchronized score"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Provide:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Original video","music version","cue sheet"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — Brand Sound Identity"},{"type":"p","text":"Create a fictional brand identity including:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sonic logo"},{"text":"10–30 second jingle"},{"text":"Brand theme"},{"text":"Advertisement music"},{"text":"Social-media sound"},{"text":"Longer brand composition"}]}]},{"heading":"Advanced Capstone Project","kind":"other","blocks":[